<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theagenes of Megara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 640–620 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theagenes was tyrant of Megara in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in the second half of the seventh century BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> he won power by championing the poor against the rich, slaughtering the flocks of wealthy landowners. He built a fountain house in the city and supported his son-in-law Cylon's failed attempt to become tyrant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> around 632 BCE.</p></div>
